0233: /dev/blueline-camera, the rear IMX363's frames for user space

ios-redfin's /dev/redwood-camera ABI (0923/0926/0931/0934, MIT,
DenialOfGravity/ios-redfin) as bsd/sys/blueline_camera.h: prefix
BLUELINE_CAMERA_, magic "BLFRAME1", same layouts and command numbers.

The first open wakes a kernel thread that runs 0196's rear path (power-up,
IMX363 2016x1512 binned RAW10, CSIPHY0, CSID-lite RDI0, IFE-lite WM0) with
the boot-arg probe's code, minus the CSID test pattern. WM0 gets a ring of
four 4 MiB buffers below 4 GiB, kept for the boot: its image address is a
two-deep queue (camss-vfe-170.c), two queued at start, one more at each
buf-done. The thread polls the latched status (bus status 1 bit 0) about
once a frame period, then every 1 ms. Queued buffers are never read; the
newest done buffer is never queued.

read() waits up to 1 s (EAGAIN) for the newest unread frame: header, then
up to stride * height bytes (2528 * 1512); a header-sized buffer gets the
header only and leaves the frame unread. EIO after a failed start or no
frame for 1 s, until the last close. write(): EXPOSURE (lines, linear gain
256 = 1x up to 8x, frame lines) in a group hold, taken after a frame and
reported from two frames later; SENSOR 1, FORMAT RAW10, FOCUS accepted;
KEEP, FLASH, COLOUR ENOTSUP. The last close ends the loop at a frame
boundary: sensor stream off, WM0 off, everything powered down as in 0196.
Line time is measured from frames 2-18. A lock keeps the boot-arg probe and
a session apart; bluecam=/bluecam_stream= behave as before. bluecamdev=0:
no device.

